{"step_index":440,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-03T15:43:43Z","thinking":"**Examining Data Synchronization Logic**\n\n`AddExpenseModal.jsx`, `AddPantryModal.jsx`, `MarketPurchaseModal.jsx`, and `SetBudgetModal.jsx` currently lack calls to a critical data update function. Proceeding to investigate which components subscribe to a data synchronization hook, to understand data flow. Specifically, inspecting `Dashboard.jsx`, it does not subscribe to the hook.\n\n\n**Implementing PKR as Default Currency**\n\nThe previous approach of fetching data after a successful mutation was insufficient for ensuring consistent data. Now, a more robust data synchronization method has been established. This ensures that the application's UI updates consistently without requiring browser refreshes.\n\nTo address the currency issue, the new functionality must support PKR. It has to become the default currency for new users and be consistently displayed across the entire application, including bills, expenses, budgets, pantry spending, totals, and summaries.\n\n\n**Analyzing Currency Implementation for PKR**\n\nThe database schema initializes `currency` to 'PKR'. Also, new user accounts default to 'PKR' during registration and profile updates. The application's `Welcome.jsx` component needs to include PKR in its currency options, as the first currency in the list, and default to 'PKR'.\n\nComponent currency display logic will need review. Currency format needs to be standardized for display of PKR, ensuring consistency with '₨' symbol regardless of the selected format, especially handling edge cases to achieve '₨' consistently. The welcome component's available currencies will be reviewed.\n\n\n**Evaluating Currency Display Consistency**\n\nCurrently, application components render currency amounts using a simple `{currency}{amount.toFixed(2)}` or `${currency} ${amount.toFixed(2)}` structure. This could lead to inconsistent formatting for PKR if '₨' isn't explicitly handled. Analyzing how `PKR` renders across various components such as `BillsRent.jsx`, `Expenses.jsx`, and others.\n\n**Developing PKR Currency Display Logic**\n\nA utility function will be created to ensure `PKR` amounts are displayed with '₨'. The function will need to determine the optimal way to include the currency symbol, whether before or after the amount, ensuring consistency. Further evaluation of the existing currency display implementation will ensure all components use this utility.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"$env:PATH = \\\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\nodejs;\\\" + $env:PATH; & \\\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\nodejs\\\\node.exe\\\" -e \\\"const db = require('./server/db/database'); const users = db.prepare('SELECT id, name, email, currency FROM users').all(); console.log('USERS:', users);\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\HP\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\household-app\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Checking existing database users and currency\"","toolSummary":"\"Inspect users table in SQLite\""}}]}
